ally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=549239#post549239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmm... you think Jigoku Shoujo could be considered a Fury?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't actually seen Jigoku Shoujo. But from what I know of it, it'd be pretty ideal. I'll have to check it out; I've heard some kids talking about it around here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T18:21:52-07:00","id":549563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=549486#post549486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ask us again after GenCon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Even if I could answer, I'm pretty much completely unqualified to address it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:40:57-07:00","id":550333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=548731#post548731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something I'd have to think on. But my gut response is, &quot;The Seers are basically humans, or at least very closely tied to them. Angels are just cogs in a machine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels have no free will - if they get some, they fall and become demons. What if the Machine doesn't have free will either - its does things according to some arcane schema, but doesn't choose anything. That means punishing it would be like trying to punish the tide.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting idea anyway.<br /> <br /> (Also interesting was the implication there's another selected game line to follow Beast).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:49:39-07:00","id":550342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=550333#post550333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels have no free will - if they get some, they fall and become demons. What if the Machine doesn't have free will either - its does things according to some arcane schema, but doesn't choose anything. That means punishing it would be like trying to punish the tide.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting idea anyway.<br /> <br /> (Also interesting was the implication there's another selected game line to follow Beast).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, and this is completely in hypothetical space -I don't want to spark a bunch of speculation when you'll hear the plans in August-, we release a major thing every year. Not always a new game line. We had Dark Eras last time around, although I believe its timeline was a little weird? But it was slated as our &quot;big summer release&quot; for NWoD last year.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, yeah. Angels are barely even sentient as far as I'm concerned. They're... just things. And the Machine doesn't have what we'd call free will. I'd consider it more in line with a force of nature. It's a more complicated gravity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:54:25-07:00","id":550455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=548422#post548422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey OP Management?<br /> <br /> Maybe you should reconsider Dave's proposal.<br /> <br /> (I also love the fact that the Furies are a supernatural a Hunter's default reaction would often be to put his arm around one and buy a beer).</div> </div> </div> </div> Well that's assuming three things.<br /> <br /> 1) The hunters realize the target had it coming. Depending on how well hidden the crimes are, quite possibly not the case.<br /> <br /> 2) The target had it coming, since Furies can be over zealous.<br /> <br /> 3) The offense is something that is actually considered offensive to modern sensibilities. I'm reminded of a quote from the Devil in Reaper to the effect of &quot;Did you know I used to get people for eating shrimp? Can you imagine how unsatisfying that was?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:04:09-07:00","id":550478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=550455#post550455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3) The offense is something that is actually considered offensive to modern sensibilities. I'm reminded of a quote from the Devil in Reaper to the effect of &quot;Did you know I used to get people for eating shrimp? Can you imagine how unsatisfying that was?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good example. If I were to do Fury as a full game, I'd want to keep those sorts of things to a minimum, but reserve them for dramatic impact. It'd definitely not be just Judeo-Christian sins, but common ideas from antiquity. But, like I note in the document, stuff like adultery is super subjective, while it wasn't so much in those times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:05:22-07:00","id":550495,"title":"","content":"Any advice if we wanted to do up Furies as a kind of minor template? Because I'm digging the idea of Furies as another bit of weirdness out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:08:27-07:00","id":550500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=550495#post550495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any advice if we wanted to do up Furies as a kind of minor template? Because I'm digging the idea of Furies as another bit of weirdness out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me give it some thought? I wouldn't mind fleshing them out just a little bit to get them into playable territory like I did with the Psychic Vampire template. But I haven't given it much consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:15:54-07:00","id":550510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=550500#post550500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me give it some thought? I wouldn't mind fleshing them out just a little bit to get them into playable territory like I did with the Psychic Vampire template. But I haven't given it much consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! That'd be great. I'd love to see whatever you've got the time and willingness to work on. I think the idea of people being empowered this way is another great little thing that could happen and make a game really interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:47:56-07:00","id":550631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=550342#post550342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, and this is completely in hypothetical space -I don't want to spark a bunch of speculation when you'll hear the plans in August-, we release a major thing every year. Not always a new game line. We had Dark Eras last time around, although I believe its timeline was a little weird? But it was slated as our &quot;big summer release&quot; for NWoD last year.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, yeah. Angels are barely even sentient as far as I'm concerned. They're... just things. And the Machine doesn't have what we'd call free will. I'd consider it more in line with a force of nature. It's a more complicated gravity.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you must have a rule saying Furies avoid the God Machine this makes a far better justification than them doing a deal IMO <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thematically the idea that the Fury's &quot;patron&quot; would ever let practical concerns get in the way of justice but ignoring the G-M because it's just a mindless machine, that makes sense. (Though I still think there's a lot of milage in Fury vs G-M games)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=550500#post550500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me give it some thought? I wouldn't mind fleshing them out just a little bit to get them into playable territory like I did with the Psychic Vampire template. But I haven't given it much consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know Fury might be better as a minor tempalte (such a shame you can't fit them into Hurt Locker). It's a very focused concept.<br /> <br /> If you want any help, I work for free <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:03:57-07:00","id":550672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=550631#post550631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you must have a rule saying Furies avoid the God Machine this makes a far better justification than them doing a deal IMO <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thematically the idea that the Fury's &quot;patron&quot; would ever let practical concerns get in the way of justice but ignoring the G-M because it's just a mindless machine, that makes sense. (Though I still think there's a lot of milage in Fury vs G-M games)</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, You can't Judge the Machine and it's Processes... but you can/could have Judged the Things that created it in the first place......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T23:24:48-07:00","id":551150,"title":"","content":"Most of the WoD games tend to be about bringing the dark into the light; giving monsters a more human side. Fury seems the opposite, taking concepts we take for granted as &quot;good&quot; (justice, karma) and dragging them into the dark. I dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T05:06:35-07:00","id":552882,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=550631#post550631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically the idea that the Fury's &quot;patron&quot; would ever let practical concerns get in the way of justice but ignoring the G-M because it's just a mindless machine, that makes sense. (Though I still think there's a lot of milage in Fury vs G-M games)</div> </div> </div> </div>Furies may believe their &quot;boss&quot; ignores the Machine because the latter's mindless, demons may believe it's because the latter is too big or impractical to take on, and angels inasmuch as they believe anything believe it <i>is</i> the boss. Other supernaturals who've heard enough about the subject to bother with an opinion usually go with whichever of these they hear first; mages of course have many more theories than that, because mages are theory-junkies (a leading one is that the Furies' boss and the Machine are both forces of order, and while they can recognise chaos as an enemy, they can't imagine a different order, and so are blind to one another).<br /> <br /> <br /> For clarity: When I said &quot;It's an interesting idea anyway,&quot; the &quot;it&quot; was referring to the Furies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T21:54:25-07:00","id":555284,"title":"","content":"Lurker here -- registered just to tell you that if you made this a full game, it'd be my favorite WoD ever. Everrrrr. Please do pitch it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6465-eleusis","name":"Eleusis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T22:30:35-07:00","id":555316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eleusis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/548001-fury-the-scourge?p=555284#post555284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lurker here -- registered just to tell you that if you made this a full game, it'd be my favorite WoD ever. Everrrrr. Please do pitch it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I'll see what I can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T22:32:05-07:00","id":555317,"title":"","content":"Given what fun Fate seem to have with Mage, Changeling, and Mummy, I'd <i>love</i> to have it take center stage in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T09:38:58-08:00","id":1002250,"title":"","content":"Oh man! I feel like there's still time to pitch that,it could work well. the theme in on point. You should try to bring it to life once more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T10:59:23-08:00","id":1002270,"title":"","content":"Given the necro, can I say something that just occurred to me?<br /> <br /> What's a Reaper's thematic deal supposed to be? The core is cool, but NPC antagonist splats have to be foils of some kind. Strix are the intellectual side of an unlife without Humanity in both boons and banes, Spirit-Claimed are the unnatural and forceful blending of worlds, Banishers are violently running from painful truths...<br /> <br /> How do they figure into the theme of vengeance, I wonder? You don't steal an artifact literally filled with one guy's rage and retribution for making the crops grow.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I can assume what this lost against is Deviant, too. Which makes sense, Deviant is a less touchy premise after the minor fiasco that was Beast. And indeed, both games are about, to some degree, revenge. And to be frank, putting the game in which you play as any experimental being you can imagine first was probably well-advised.<br /> <br /> But a Fury seems to be different enough to be their own thing-by definition, they've finished their first revenge, and now seek it for others, or for Fate, or really anyone but them. A Deviant fights authority, a Fury, to an extent, <i>is </i>an authority figure (I'd expect de-linking from the God-Machine, but a Fury having a choir of minions at their beck and call for implementing their agenda and orders from Providence is something I doubt will be dropped). That's something new to both worlds, I think (except Mummy, and the Arisen cults are cultists worshiping a god they don't always get along with rather than inhuman minions that may not understand mercy or nuance).<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Also, a big problem that needs doing is figuring out a way to prevent (too much) railroading, despite, y'know, literally being agents of rather stubborn Fate and following its disturbances. Probably needs more things to do than just &quot;investigate disturbances, gauge punishment, deal with consequences&quot; as well. This isn't Deviant, where the whole point is matching wits with a custom conspiracy, and thus the players actually made the story they want to tell themselves (maybe Fate can be disturbed in other ways...and maybe Furies can use their position to &quot;advise&quot; Fate, for OOC agency and IC extra tension about the hard decisions of what to do when you're functionally a lobbyist in the Celestial Bureaucracy). And Furies need their own culture above Choruses as well-perhaps not Social Splats, but they definitely need ways in how they interact with themselves across the world, chat about tips, and block each other from overly cruel punishments (to their subjective opinion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-12-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}